tity. These conditions include meeting a debt service coverage ratio prior to distribution, which was met by these entities in the first quarter of 2026, with the exception of Windrise Wind LP. The funds in Windrise that have accumulated will remain there until the debt-service coverage ratio distribution threshold is met. At March 31, 2026, $9 million (AU$9 million) of funds held by TEC Hedland Pty Ltd. cannot be accessed by other corporate entities as the funds must be solely used by the project entities and to pay major maintenance costs. Additionally, certain non-recourse bonds require that certain reserve accounts be established and funded through cash held on deposit and/or by providing letters of credit. C. Restricted Cash As at March 31, 2026, the Company had nil (Dec. 31, 2025 \u2013 $17 million) of restricted cash related to the TransAlta OCP bonds, which is required to be held in a debt service reserve account in the third and fourth quarters of the year to fund scheduled future debt repayments. The Company also had $4\n"}
